            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "'mini.snippets' is designed to integrate with 'rafamadriz/friendly-snippets' as smoothly as possible while being flexible enough in how it can load snippets. In practice, having the [following setup](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3a354c754656538ad76d1add93ca21e75b7f3181/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L379-L390) is usually enough for common languages in 'friendly-snippets'.\r\n\r\nAs for 'Saghen/blink.cmp', see [this](https://github.com/Saghen/blink.cmp/blob/main/doc/configuration/snippets.md). I don't use it and don't have much experience with it.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">'mini.snippets' is designed to integrate with 'rafamadriz/friendly-snippets' as smoothly as possible while being flexible enough in how it can load snippets. In practice, having the <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3a354c754656538ad76d1add93ca21e75b7f3181/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L379-L390\">following setup</a> is usually enough for common languages in 'friendly-snippets'.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As for 'Saghen/blink.cmp', see <a href=\"https://github.com/Saghen/blink.cmp/blob/main/doc/configuration/snippets.md\">this</a>. I don't use it and don't have much experience with it.</p>",
